WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
The state of Zhao had a famous treasure jade called the He Shi Bi.

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.382
When the King of Qin heard of it, he wanted very much to have it.

00:00:07.732 --> 00:00:11.524
The He Shi Bi was flawless white jade, a treasure famed throughout the world.

00:00:11.874 --> 00:00:15.306
The King of Qin said he was willing to trade fifteen cities for the jade.

00:00:15.656 --> 00:00:19.208
The King of Zhao feared a trick, and Lin Xiangru volunteered to go as envoy to Qin.

00:00:19.558 --> 00:00:22.918
Lin Xiangru brought the He Shi Bi to the court of Qin.

00:00:23.268 --> 00:00:26.700
The King of Qin held the jade and happily showed it to everyone.

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:30.698
The King of Qin only gazed at the jade, never mentioning the cities at all.

00:00:31.048 --> 00:00:33.976
Lin Xiangru saw that the King of Qin had no intention of trading the cities.

00:00:34.326 --> 00:00:38.286
Pretending to point out a flaw on the jade, he took it back into his hands.

00:00:38.636 --> 00:00:41.876
Though the King of Qin was angry, he could not lose his temper on the spot.

00:00:42.226 --> 00:00:45.874
Lin Xiangru sent a man with the jade to return secretly to Zhao.

00:00:46.224 --> 00:00:49.512
He himself stayed in Qin, bravely facing the King of Qin.

00:00:49.862 --> 00:00:52.742
Knowing the jade was already gone, the King of Qin had to let him return.

00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:55.612
In the end, the He Shi Bi returned to Zhao completely intact.

00:00:55.962 --> 00:00:59.202
"Returning the jade intact to Zhao" means returning something whole to its owner.

00:00:59.552 --> 00:01:02.480
His courage and wisdom protected his country's dignity.

